   {
    "primary": {
     "type": "TextChapter",
     "page_section_element_title": [],
     "page_section_element_body": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "The design system is the documentation of all the digital resources, elements, and instructions, that make up Aalto University’s digital sites and services. It serves as a framework that helps maintain a consistent user experience throughout all digital services and touchpoints, ultimately contributing both to the university's brand identity and user satisfaction.",
       "spans": []
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "The design system consists of reusable design assets, component libraries, and guidelines. A shared set of design guidelines and elements enables the teams to work more efficiently, facilitating collaboration among different teams and departments within the university. This leads to faster and more consistent design iterations and content development and helps avoid user experience fragmentation.",
       "spans": []
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "text": "The pre-designed set of components provided by the design system adheres to various accessibility guidelines related to colour contrast, typography, and navigation. This approach guarantees that all of Aalto University's digital touchpoints are usable by everyone, irrespective of their abilities or assistive technologies.",
       "spans": []
      }
     ],
     "component_id": null,
